WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.950
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this is going
to be my Jon Snow video.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.010
I’m expecting the show to catch up with
his story in the books so what I think I’m

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:20.869
gonna do is start with what’s going on right
as Season 5 picks up, what we know about him

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:25.100
just based on the trailer and then put him
into perspective with the other characters.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.230
I guess you could call this video the progression
of Snow.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.020
Which seems like a nice Winter is Coming joke.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.930
Also, the giveaway this week just got upgraded.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.800
I am giving away a copy of the Season 4 Blu
Ray.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.440
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.730
More details at the end of the video.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.920
Careful for spoilers through season 4 on the
show.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.070
Starting at the end of Season 4.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.799
The last we see of him is cleaning up the
mess of bodies from the Siege of Castle Black.

00:00:54.799 --> 00:01:02.649
They burn all the bodies, not because they
totally buy into the idea of White Walkers

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:07.960
and the Great Other, but because it’s practical
and most of them are probably really superstitious.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.990
Melisandre is there now and she has this really
scary charisma, she’s all about preparing

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.980
for the war with the great other.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.120
So I don’t think it matters whether or not
anyone believes in white walkers.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.360
I think they’ll be more afraid of her and
Stannis.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.660
There’s all the wildlings that surrendered.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.890
Now they have to figure out what to do with
them.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.990
And based on what we saw in the trailer, there’s
a whole other group of Wildlings holed up

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.570
in Hardhome up here that they’ll have to
deal with.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.560
It seems like the tv show is going to stay
pretty close to the big beats of books 4 and

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.560
5.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.500
Most of what happens up at the wall is Book
5 anyway.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.040
So if you want to follow that directly in
the books.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.770
You need to jump from the end of book 3 to
book 5.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:54.270
Cersei thinks about the Night’s Watch in
her Book 4 POV chapters, but the actual story

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.020
up there is all book 5.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.380
What do all these things mean for Jon Snow?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.110
Everyone in a position of leadership have
different agendas, so all the big problems

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.440
get dumped on him to deal with.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:19.900
The biggest characters he has to contend with
are Stannis and Melisande, then inside the

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.680
Night’s Watch there’s Alliser Thorne,
Janos Slynt,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:33.019
Amongst the Wildlings there’s Mance Rayder
and Tormund Giantsbane both captives, so not

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.510
quite as big of a threat.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.840
Rattleshirt is back too but based on this
clip in the trailer it’s hard to tell whether

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.510
or not he was part of Mance’s captured army
or if he’s part of the group up at Hardhome.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.060
This new character, Loboda definitely looks
like he’s part of the Hardhome group.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.040
So as much as Stannis and the Night’s Watch
defeated Mance Rayder’s army.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.829
The Wildling’s are still a huge issue to
be dealt with before everyone can start worrying

00:02:54.829 --> 00:02:57.249
about the White Walkers and The Boltons to
the south.

00:02:57.249 --> 00:03:00.889
I think the show is pushing for some narrative
symmetry between Jon and Daenerys.

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:03.819
Two people who are falling into leadership
positions without being completely ready for

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:04.819
it.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.200
Daenerys is a more obvious example because
she’s sitting on a real throne.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:15.840
I don’t think it’s a spoiler for endgame
or anything like that, just because these

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.659
quote unquote fire and ice characters are
on similar trajectories doesn’t guarantee

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:24.560
they’ll both live forever.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:33.059
Part of the fun of Song of Ice and Fire is
that anyone can be killed off at any time

00:03:33.059 --> 00:03:35.209
for any reason.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:45.959
But I do think in Season 5, Jon and Daenerys
will hit a lot of the same beats.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.829
That’s really as far as it goes right now
though.

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:50.859
They both have very different motivations.

00:03:50.859 --> 00:04:03.329
When the season starts, the key things to
watch will be Jon’s new leadership role

00:04:03.329 --> 00:04:16.890
and 
how that changes his dynamic with Stannis

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.040
and the other senior Members of the Night’s
Watch.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.810
Jon’s relationship with Melisandre and the
creepy plans it seems like she has for him.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:31.000
And Jon’s relationship with his family.With
Winterfell.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:36.230
I’m curious if in the opening title sequence,
Winterfell will still be blackened and burning.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.730
I mean really, it would have stopped burning
a long time ago.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:42.700
The fact it’s still burning every week in
the intro is just a reminder of what happened

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.700
to it.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.650
It’s not quite as bad off as Harrenhal was
after Aegon sent his dragons to destroy it.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.370
But large parts of it were burned.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:53.570
That’s actually a good place to get into
book stuff.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.690
There’s a lot of interesting Winterfell
dragon related theories but let’s talk about

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.850
some of the Jon Snow changes the show might
be making.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:06.280
Just looking at the trailer, it seems like
they gave Jon Cotter Pyke’s story and sent

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.600
him to Hardhome to deal with the crazy wildlings.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.980
There’s a whole crazy history of Hardhome
that sounds a lot like what happened at Jamestown

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:13.980
in real life.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:18.460
Jamestown was an early american colony where
everyone mysteriously died or disappeared.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:29.440
They even found evidence of cannibalism.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:34.480
Hardhome in the books invokes a lot of mystical
supernatural aspects in that sense, but the

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.480
outcome was the same.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:41.300
The town was labeled as haunted and wildlings
never went there again, until now.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:47.310
I’ll have to do a separate video for Hardhome
when we see it on the show.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.130
It’s a really cool story.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:53.850
If Jon is able to win over the Wildlings there
and bring them back it would win him more

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.480
support from Stannis.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:06:02.840
As it is, he doesn’t seem like he gives
a lot of respect to bastards.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.440
Even if they’re the bastards of Ned Stark.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.440
Supposedly.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.800
That brings up a question I don’t see asked
a as much.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.580
For those that have not read the books, before
he died, Robb Stark legitimized Jon Snow.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:15.580
That means he’s a proper heir of Winterfell.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:16.580
As of Season 3.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.510
They didn’t include this on the show, so
I’m going to assume they’re not ever going

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.470
to bring it up.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.560
Right now Sansa is the rightful heir.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:27.850
And if you believe Littlefinger, he’s going
to try and get it back for her.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:31.510
As much as Jon has his shit together up at
the wall, it’s the love of his family that

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:35.080
makes him want to break his oath and ride
for the Boltons.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:41.210
The Jeyne Pool stand-in character Myranda
is back in season 5.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.540
So I wonder if Ramsay will send Jon a false
letter claiming they have Arya.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:48.570
If you look at this map here, it seems like
Stannis is mapping Bolton troop locations.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:55.090
So they are doing that part of the book, but
they might swap a few of the characters.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:07:00.480
I think the plot up at the wall will be the
closest to the books of any of the running

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.480
storylines.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.950
They’ll all have minor changes but just
in descending order from Least Changed to

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:03.950
most changed.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:09.531
I’d say Jon Snow slash North, King’s Landing
Cersei stuff, Daenerys in Meereen, Arya in

00:07:09.531 --> 00:07:15.940
Braavos and kind of a tie for most-changed
between Tyrion and the Dorne stuff.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.580
Those two storylines have massive chunks and
major characters missing.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.293
When we get to those episodes I’ll include
a list of big changes in my videos.

00:07:23.293 --> 00:07:24.293
I try to not plan ahead too much because usually
I don’t know how many of you are book readers

00:07:24.293 --> 00:07:25.293
and how many just watch the show.

00:07:25.293 --> 00:07:29.650
If there are any big changes you guys want
to talk about specifically just let me know.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:34.310
I know cutting out Young Griff is a big deal,
but I think a lot of the story they lost will

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:36.080
be given to other characters.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.800
Just like giving Edric Storm’s story to
Gendry.

